WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:06.600
Hi! Today you learn separable verbs.

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.800
These verbs split into two parts!

3
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.932
This is my day:

4
00:00:15.332 --> 00:00:18.076
I get up at seven.

5
00:00:18.476 --> 00:00:21.748
Work starts at nine.

6
00:00:22.148 --> 00:00:25.348
In the afternoon I go shopping.

7
00:00:25.748 --> 00:00:28.900
Then I call my mother.

8
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.116
In the evening I watch TV.

9
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:38.080
The first part jumps to the end of the sentence:

10
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.944
aufstehen: I get up.

11
00:00:42.344 --> 00:00:45.352
I get up at seven.

12
00:00:45.752 --> 00:00:48.184
When do you get up?

13
00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:55.980
How do you recognise a separable verb? The stress is at the front:

14
00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:00.612
EINkaufen, ANrufen, FERNsehen.

15
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:07.300
Listen: what do Lena and Mateo do on Sunday?

16
00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.828
When do you get up on Sunday?

17
00:01:11.228 --> 00:01:14.308
Not until ten!

18
00:01:14.708 --> 00:01:16.780
And then?

19
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:20.260
I call my family.

20
00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:23.068
Do you go shopping too?

21
00:01:23.468 --> 00:01:27.172
No, everything's closed on Sunday!

22
00:01:28.867 --> 00:01:36.987
Now you! Describe your day with aufstehen, einkaufen, anrufen and fernsehen.

23
00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:52.836
Great! Now you can:

24
00:01:53.236 --> 00:01:58.740
You know separable verbs: the first part jumps to the end.

25
00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:01.260
See you soon!
